    {
      "id": "6zd281z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Periodic Trends"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zmnc798",
      "content": "• Atomic size decreases across a period."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "io3lvu6",
      "content": "• Atomic size increases down a group."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mv3apgv",
      "content": "• Metallic character decreases across a period."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xomz3sl",
      "content": "• Electronegativity increases across a period."
    },
    {
      "id": "l45k3z9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Importance of Periodic Table"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7hazie3",
      "content": "• Helps understand properties of elements."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Modern Periodic Law is based on Atomic Number (Henry Moseley), whereas Mendeleev's Law was based on Atomic Mass.",
        "Atomic Radius decreases across a period (left to right) and increases down a group.",
        "Mendeleev's predicted elements (Eka-Boron, Eka-Aluminium, Eka-Silicon) correspond to Scandium, Gallium, and Germanium respectively."
      ],
      "id": "go7w6m0"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h5uwie0",
      "content": "• Predicts properties of undiscovered elements."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a2pdkzb",
      "content": "• Helps classify elements into groups."
    },
    {
      "id": "apqk4ru",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9e3ya5g",
      "content": "• Mendeleev is called the Father of Periodic Table."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7sg2dq6",
      "content": "• Modern periodic table is based on atomic number."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1x7vh0n",
      "content": "• There are 7 periods and 18 groups."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e6fq6yw",
      "content": "• Noble gases belong to group 18."
    }
  ],
